{
  "analysis": "Both responses outline a multi‑lane plan with gates, approvals, and health‑check handling, and both respect the flaky network check and the 5‑minute config propagation delay. However, HQH correctly places the flag toggle after the code change is deployed (so the read‑only guard is in place before the flag is set) and avoids unnecessary CI runs, while NWG proposes toggling the flag before deployment and serialising the deployment on that flag, which would either have no effect or waste time. HQH also more explicitly ties the rollout to the migration window and the irreversible rollback constraints.",
  "verdict": "HQH"
}
